<!--Render Target Documentation — ExpressionRenderer
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.ExpressionRenderer-->
<rdoc:ExpressionRenderer xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Expression values to SCAD expressions
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Canonical BOM stores expressions as ExpressionValue { raw }. The expression
    renderer obtains a typed AST via parseExpression() (a working-model utility,
    not a canonical BOM field) and serializes it to SCAD.

    Static: if the expression has no runtime-dependent roots, emit the resolved
    value. ${ [1, 1, 1] } becomes [1, 1, 1].

    Dynamic: if it references block properties or bml:with variables, emit a
    SCAD expression. StructType members are addressed by name in BML. The
    expression language rejects a numeric index on a StructType (size[0]).
    A collection index (items[0]) stays an index.

    When the property's SCAD form is a positional array, a named member becomes
    the declaration-order index of that field. That is the default StructType
    serialization and the V1 path. SizeXYZ declares x, y, z, so:

        ${ [size.x, size.y, size.z - 1] }
          -> [size[0], size[1], size[2] - 1]
        ${ #math.max(size.z - 1, 0) }
          -> max(size[2] - 1, 0)

    When the property's SCAD form is an OpenSCAD object, the member stays
    name.member. That form belongs to the future object() settings emitter.

    Root mapping:

    - myProperty -> SCAD local variable of that name
    - myProperty.member on an array-form value -> name[declarationOrdinal]
    - myProperty.member on an object-form value -> name.member
    - items[i] on a collection -> items[i]
    - withVariable -> SCAD local from the bml:with scope
    - #math.min(a, b) / #math.max(a, b) -> min / max via the native map

    A list element keeps the element type. An enum member on a typed field
    resolves to the catalog token when a sibling field is dynamic. WallGap
    face: Y in [{face: Y, len: size.z - 1}] emits "y". A missing pos is 0,
    the same shape as a constant WallGap.

    V1 does not execute @bean calls or model bindings as SCAD. A TypeScript
    implementation whose arguments are all literals is evaluated at compile
    time and emitted as that literal. Any other @bean call is not emitted;
    the diagnostic is BML_FUNCTION_NO_RUNTIME_IMPL. OpenSCAD capability
    implementations (FQN-prefixed functions) are a later processor and are
    not required for V1 block and set emit.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:AssemblyPatterns" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:ExpressionRenderer>
